# Meldungen aus dem Rust-Teil, die früher als deutsche Festtexte im Quelltext standen (Anwender sichtbar). Katalogpflege: i18n-i2.
rest-cond-size-nicht-verfuegbar = size() is not available here
rest-cond-anfuehrungszeichen = Unclosed quotation mark
rest-cond-size-segmentname = size() expects the segment name in quotation marks
rest-debug-mega65-rom = MEGA65 ROM not found
rest-debug-speicher-nicht-lesbar = Memory cannot be read
rest-debug-kein-einzelschritt = This adapter does not support single stepping
rest-debug-emulator-laeuft = The emulator is running – pause it first
rest-debug-kein-ruecksprung-5s = The subroutine does not return (within 5 s)
rest-debug-kein-ruecksprung-10s = No return within 10 s (loop in the subroutine?) – set a breakpoint at the return
rest-listen-kein-programm-chip = There is no player program for this song ({ $channels } voices on chip “{ $chip }”).
rest-listen-pokey = There is no player program for POKEY songs (Atari) on the Ultimate yet; they only play through the synthesizer.
rest-listen-mega65 = The song has twelve voices for the MEGA65; the Ultimate 64 only plays C64 programs with the 3-voice SID.
rest-listen-plus4 = The song is for the TED of the Plus/4; the Ultimate 64 has no TED.
rest-listen-vic20 = The song is for the VIC of the VIC-20; the Ultimate 64 does not have this sound chip.
rest-listen-profil = There is no player program for the profile “{ $p }”.
rest-livebild-wartezeit = No complete image was received within the waiting time.
rest-roms-os-xl = atari8/os-xl: not in the ROM folder – atari800 uses its own setting or the built-in Altirra OS (replacement)
rest-roms-mega65-revision = mega65/rom: unknown revision, symbols and offsets may differ
rest-roms-altirra = Altirra manages its firmware itself (Altirra settings); VintageCoder passes no ROMs
rest-streams-kein-empfaenger = no receiver was given for the packets
rest-streams-ausgefallen = Stream lost: no packet has arrived for more than 2 seconds (device off, cable unplugged or the stream ended in the Ultimate).
rest-streams-multicast-an = 4. Multicast: some switches and Wi-Fi access points do not forward multicast; if in doubt, turn multicast off in the settings.
rest-streams-multicast-aus = 4. Nothing helps: try multicast in the settings as a way out.
rest-platzhalter-project-label = Project name
rest-platzhalter-project-hint = Name of the project (folder name)
rest-platzhalter-project-dir-label = Project folder
rest-platzhalter-project-dir-hint = Absolute path of the project folder
rest-platzhalter-output-label = Output file
rest-platzhalter-output-hint = The built program (PRG, XEX, CRT, …) that is started
rest-platzhalter-target-label = Target system
rest-platzhalter-target-hint = Identifier of the target system: c64, c128, plus4, vic20, atari8, mega65
rest-platzhalter-variant-label = Video standard
rest-platzhalter-variant-hint = pal or ntsc (Atari: from the project file, otherwise pal)
rest-platzhalter-start-label = Start address
rest-platzhalter-start-hint = Entry point from the BASIC starter (SYS) as four hex digits, e.g. 080D; only if the program has one
rest-platzhalter-symbols-label = Symbol file
rest-platzhalter-symbols-hint = Labels for the monitor (VICE: .vs next to the output file); only after a build
rest-platzhalter-disk-label = Disk image
rest-platzhalter-disk-hint = The disk image of the project (disk field of the project file); only if the project has one
